course: dictionary
lesson: 11501
title: Agrarian: words about farming
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Agrarian is a word you will meet in history and geography. It describes things linked to farming and farmland. Look for the clues around it. «The village is agrarian, and most families grow wheat and keep cows.» Growing wheat and keeping cows are farm jobs, so agrarian must mean about farming.
explain: Agrarian describes a noun, like a society, an economy or a village. «In an agrarian society, most people work on the land.» Here the society is the whole group of people, and the word tells you that most of them farm. If you swap in farming for agrarian and the sentence still makes sense, your meaning is right.
explain: Some phrases you will see are «agrarian society», «agrarian economy» and «agrarian reform». Each one is about farming or farmland. When you meet a new phrase, read the words around it first, then check a dictionary if you are still unsure.
fact: Agrarian means about farming, farmland or the people who work on the land.
fact: Agrarian is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as society, economy or village.
fact: An «agrarian society» is one that lives mainly by farming.
fact: «Agrarian reform» is a change to how farmland is shared out or worked.
exercise: «Most families in the valley grow wheat and keep cows, so it is an agrarian area.» What does agrarian mean here? | About trains and cities | *About farming and farmland | About the sea and boats | About schools and books
exercise: Which place is most agrarian? | *A village where most people grow crops | A busy city with tall office blocks | A town by the sea full of boats | A station with trains every minute
exercise: Why would a history book call a country agrarian? | *Most people there live by farming | Most people there never work at all | Most people there live in tall buildings | Most people there work on ships
test: «Agrarian reform changed how the farmland was shared out.» What does agrarian mean in this sentence? | About the ocean | About factories | *About farmland | About the city
test: Which phrase means a society that lives mainly by farming? | *agrarian society | busy harbour | ancient castle | silent forest
exam: Finish the sentence: An agrarian economy depends mostly on | shops | ships | *farming | banks
